## 5.4 L-cross function

Aside from the point event pattern of the individual F&B business types, we can also perform hypothesis testing to test the spatial relationship between the individual F&B business types. The hypotheses for this are as follows:

-   H~0~: The two point types are independent of each other

-   H~1~: The two point types are not independent of each other

    -   If L~i,j~(r) is positive, this indicates there is a positive association between point types, i.e., the points are clustered around each other

    -   If L~i,j,~(r) is negative, this indicates there is a negative association between point types, i.e., the points are dispersed or repelled from each other.

As above, we use `envelope()` to perform Monte Carlo simulation for this exercise.

::: panel-tabset
#### Cafes & Food Stalls

```{r}
#| eval: false
L_c_fs.csr <- envelope(fnb_cr_ppp.km, Lcross, 
                       nsim=99, 
                       i="Cafes", j="Food Stalls",
                       rank=1,
                       glocal=TRUE)
```

```{r}
#| echo: false
#| eval: false
